{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468548-mega-stamina-regeneration","id":1468548,"title":"Mega stamina regeneration","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: Aberrant"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-11-21T19:22:56-08:00","id":1468548,"title":"Mega stamina regeneration","content":"I'm the mega edge regeneration it states that a nova could regenerate his brain but I'm curious how a nova could survive his brain been destroyed. Is this something that could come from a high mega stamina rating, a mega edge, or something else. Could I get everyone's take on this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T19:32:19-08:00","id":1468549,"title":"","content":"The nova don\u2019t need to survive to regenerate. They can die, as long they have quantum they will regenerate, or at least as long the damage cease, the nova can regenerate. To keep the Nova dead you need to drive the body somewhere the damage keep the body destroyed.<br /> <br /> Remember that Taken out means stop fighting, not dead, but can also mean dead to start regenerating again.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T21:56:39-08:00","id":1468561,"title":"","content":"Do they become braindead? What's the in universe explanation for how their consciousness remains intact in such a situation?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T22:22:42-08:00","id":1468563,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Planguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468548-mega-stamina-regeneration?p=1468561#post1468561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do they become braindead? What's the in universe explanation for how their consciousness remains intact in such a situation?</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't give an in-universe explanation but if you want/need one, you can take or alter mine: <i>&quot;The nova's physiology regenerates their body &amp; mind from a blueprint of their healthy self-image their subconscious imprints into local space/time at a quantum level&quot;.</i><br /> <br /> It's complete hand-wavium, but it doesn't clash with anything in the lore and even provides an interesting explanation for nova Transformations (at eruption &amp; from later Transcendence) - their Transformations are part of their subconscious self-image and therefore their regeneration &quot;heals&quot; them transformed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-21T22:58:25-08:00","id":1468569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Planguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468548-mega-stamina-regeneration?p=1468561#post1468561\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do they become braindead? What's the in universe explanation for how their consciousness remains intact in such a situation?</div> </div> </div> </div>From the moment of eruption, novas are no longer \u2018human\u2019, they\u2019re a living Quantum flux zone. Flesh, blood, brains, are just remnants of a new state of being that hasn\u2019t got around to transcending them yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-22T03:10:57-08:00","id":1468578,"title":"","content":"Remembering that Biokinesis have a similar effect, and Vitakinesis can restore brain dead people to life.<br /> <br /> You don\u2019t need to have a technical explanation, the workings of super powers are beyond natural limits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-22T05:40:09-08:00","id":1468584,"title":"","content":"That's pretty cool, so the general take is a nova with regeneration can heal from anything even &quot;Death&quot; as long as they have the required quantum points. I'm curious as to what ideas people have for adding tags to regeneration to make it stronger or fit it to a theme or concept for their character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26058-aeonstorm","name":"Aeonstorm","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-22T06:14:49-08:00","id":1468588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mateus Luz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468548-mega-stamina-regeneration?p=1468578#post1468578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Remembering that Biokinesis have a similar effect, and Vitakinesis can restore brain dead people to life.<br /> <br /> You don\u2019t need to have a technical explanation, the workings of super powers are beyond natural limits.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> And Healing can, within a certain amount of time with enough successes, also heal someone who is brain dead, or even had no head... so obviously there's something going on that goes beyond the obvious understanding. Now the REALLY interesting question is... are there potentially multiple noetic versions of that person at once if such happens? Like, let's say a telepath creates a noetic copy... but their body dies... then is brought back with quantum powers... is there multiple versions? Is this a &quot;branching&quot; thing, or do they synch up as the same person?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr />\u200bWhen noise turns to silence, when colors dull and pale, when reality no longer makes sense, there shall you find me. There, in the dreams of the River of Faceless Millions, do I dwell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/\" target=\"_blank\">http://harenm.deviantart.com/gallery/</a> for my art.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/378-haren","name":"haren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar378_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"664"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-22T06:19:23-08:00","id":1468589,"title":"","content":"If you cut a body in the middle, can you heal each part to make 2 copies? Maybe one using VK and another using Healing to prevent the \u201cnoetic syncing\u201d or something like that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-22T12:41:52-08:00","id":1468622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>haren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468548-mega-stamina-regeneration?p=1468588#post1468588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">let's say a telepath creates a noetic copy... but their body dies... then is brought back with quantum powers... is there multiple versions?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope, there\u2019s just a dead telepath because Quantum and psi don\u2019t mix and their noetic copy is scrambled.<br /> <br /> But from a point of view where something like this was possible, also no. The noetic template allows for one \u2018prime\u2019 instance on an individual, even with BK cloning. As long as the prime is around, you don\u2019t get a second prime.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-22T18:10:43-08:00","id":1468644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eternl Knight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468548-mega-stamina-regeneration?p=1468563#post1468563\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They don't give an in-universe explanation but if you want/need one, you can take or alter mine: <i>&quot;The nova's physiology regenerates their body &amp; mind from a blueprint of their healthy self-image their subconscious imprints into local space/time at a quantum level&quot;.</i><br /> <br /> It's complete hand-wavium, but it doesn't clash with anything in the lore and even provides an interesting explanation for nova Transformations (at eruption &amp; from later Transcendence) - their Transformations are part of their subconscious self-image and therefore their regeneration &quot;heals&quot; them transformed.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Isn't that a more noetic thing? Sub-quantum powers always seemed more about being in tune with the universe and effecting things by manipulating them through their sub-quantum pattern, or whatever it's called. I though quantum powers were more about making gross changes rather then subtle ones.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27133-planguy","name":"Planguy","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-22T18:49:48-08:00","id":1468648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Planguy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-aberrant/1468548-mega-stamina-regeneration?p=1468644#post1468644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Isn't that a more noetic thing? Sub-quantum powers always seemed more about being in tune with the universe and effecting things by manipulating them through their sub-quantum pattern, or whatever it's called. I though quantum powers were more about making gross changes rather then subtle ones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, ignoring the fact I'm keenly aware of my explanation being pure hand-wavium at a level that would make most anime blush - quantum powers are able to manipulate space-time (think teleportation &amp; warp powers) AND can manipulate stuff all the way down to the quark level.<br /> <br /> So, to delve deeper into the realms of imaginarian science, perhaps the nova quantum entangles a functional blueprint of their physiology written in quarks &amp; leptons at the point in space-time they erupted. Their subconscious updates that blueprint slowly over time as their self-image changes and their powers read back from that blueprint when healing their physical body. Their memories &amp; thought processed are actually stored in the same location as a nanoscopic quantum computer, all wrapped in a fold of space-time created to protect the nova's quantum phylactery from harm. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Seriously though, we've got the official explanation from Bunyip (one of the devs) and it's just as good as any other explanation out there. Living Quantum flux zone... which can mean pretty much whatever you like as long as you flavour it with the &quot;Quantum&quot; and &quot;flux&quot; keywords. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26905-eternl-knight","name":"Eternl Knight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26905_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"106"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T11:13:34-08:00","id":1469343,"title":"","content":"So can you cancel regen if you take the body into a quantum-free zone, or use a quantum-shutdown power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2678-spoonr","name":"SpoonR","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2678_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-12-01T15:32:28-08:00","id":1469368,"title":"","content":"You reflexively spend Quantum points to Regenerate so a Quantum free zone wouldn't stop them unless it also inhibited a Nova from spending points.<br /> <br /> Quantum Drain would allow you to take all of their Quantum points which would stop the Regen.<br /> <br /> Quantum Shutdown is a trickier thing though. It says it will shutdown quantum powers, but Regeneration isn't a power it's a Mega-Edge. While it costs Quantum to use it isn't in the powers section. <br /> I have no idea as to the official ruling on that so it's either post in Ask the Devs and see if one of them knows or leave it up to the Storyteller.<br /> In my game I would say no, Quantum Shutdown wouldn't stop Regeneration but that is just my personal opinion on it.<br /> <br /> However the easiest way to kill a Nova with Regeneration is keep hitting them. Once they run out of Quantum points they stop Regenerating and die. The method to recover Quantum points require a scene change to work so as long as any damage is being applied they will run out of points sooner or later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27184-darrendalca","name":"DarrenDalca","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27184_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}